{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0097562","isObsolete":false,"name":"left lateral basal body pair","definition":{"text":"Set of two basal bodies found in Giardia species (trophozoite stage). It comprises the anterior and ventral basal bodies located to the right of the left nucleus of the trophozoite when viewed dorsally.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"ISBN","dbId":"9780124260207"},{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"16607022"},{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"5961344"}]},"comment":"Due to the asymmetric nature of the Giardia trophozoite, this term is defined spatially as the trophozoite is viewed from the dorsal side, with the two nuclei dorsal to the ventral disc, and the ventral disc toward the anterior.","history":[{"timestamp":"2019-09-12","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0110165 (cellular anatomical structure)"},{"timestamp":"2019-09-12","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044463 (obsolete cell projection part)"},{"timestamp":"2019-09-12","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0042995 (cell projection)"},{"timestamp":"2015-12-09","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-07","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044463 (obsolete cell projection part)"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-07","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"Set of two basal bodies found in Giardia species (trophozoite stage). It comprises the anterior and ventral basal bodies located to the right of the left nucleus of the trophozoite when viewed dorsally."},{"timestamp":"2014-02-07","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"left lateral basal body pair"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-07","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"has part GO:0097566 (left tetrad)"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0097562","ancestorName":"left lateral basal body pair","relationship":"only_in_taxon","taxId":"5738","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Diplomonadida"}],"aspect":"cellular_component","usage":"Unrestricted"}],"pageInfo":null}